// An ordering comparison with a DECIMAL on both sides.
//
// Ordering is defined on integers only. The guide: ordering "requires both sides to resolve to
// integers; otherwise the comparison is false", and a decimal "resolves but fails the integer
// conversion and yields false". So this gate never opens, however large the score.
//
// Our model ordered decimals by their scaled value until 2026-09-11 -- 9000 > 5000 -- and said
// ALLOW. A wrong verdict, not a missing feature. No corpus case compares a decimal with an
// ordering operator, so 919 agreeing pairs said nothing about it; the engine settled it.
//
// BOTH SIDES MUST BE DECIMAL for this to discriminate. `s > 0` against a decimal column already
// fails on the kind check, so it would pass with or without the fix -- which is exactly what the
// first version of this fixture did.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Anchor::Action::"Trade",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    exists (s: Long). (
        formerly within 1h Anchor::Action::"Score"::response{ output.score: s }
        && s > decimal("0.5")
    )
};
